/F1 12 Tf
72 740 Td
(Dear Diary,) Tj
72 724 Td (I promised myself I would be brave today.) Tj
72 708 Td (So I marched into the library wearing my heroic scarf.) Tj
72 692 Td (The scarf immediately fell into a fountain.) Tj
72 676 Td (I pretended the fountain needed hydration and saluted it.) Tj
72 660 Td (To recover my dignity, I announced a fox parade.) Tj
72 644 Td (Two pigeons joined. We formed a marching band.) Tj
72 628 Td (The pigeons played jazz. I played confidence.) Tj
72 612 Td (Halfway through, a squirrel challenged me to a duel.) Tj
72 596 Td (We agreed the first to blink would lose.) Tj
72 580 Td (A leaf fell dramatically. We both blinked at once.) Tj
72 564 Td (The squirrel declared a tie and offered trail mix.) Tj
72 548 Td (I accepted, because diplomacy is my greatest weapon.) Tj
72 532 Td (At lunch I ordered a fancy salad and the waiter was a bee.) Tj
72 516 Td (He said the dressing was strictly royal and wore a tiny crown.) Tj
72 500 Td (I nodded like a noble, but the crown made me nervous.) Tj
72 484 Td (Later I wrote a poem to the moon about bravery.) Tj
72 468 Td (The moon replied with a parking ticket for my tail.) Tj
72 452 Td (Apparently there is a no-hover zone in the sky now.) Tj
72 436 Td (I tried to argue, but the ticket was very official.) Tj
72 420 Td (I practiced a dramatic sigh in the mirror.) Tj
72 404 Td (The mirror sighed back and scared me so much) Tj
72 388 Td (that I bowed, slipped, and bowed deeper for respect.) Tj
72 372 Td (I attempted a stealthy exit, yet my stomach growled) Tj
72 356 Td (like thunder. The thunder said it was my fan club.) Tj
72 340 Td (So I bowed again. I am nothing if not polite.) Tj
72 324 Td (Then I tripped on a heroic root and apologized.) Tj
72 308 Td (The tree forgave me and called me a legend.) Tj
72 292 Td (I nearly cried, but heroes do not cry in public.) Tj
72 276 Td (To look cool I leaned on a wall, but it was a door) Tj
72 260 Td (and I fell into a meeting about acorn taxes.) Tj
72 244 Td (I voted yes because everyone looked serious.) Tj
72 228 Td (If anyone asks, I was never there.) Tj
72 212 Td (I was a rumor wearing a damp heroic scarf.) Tj
72 196 Td (Please pretend you never read this.) Tj
72 180 Td (I am definitely cool and not flustered.) Tj
72 164 Td (End of entry. Hide the diary under the fern.) Tj
72 148 Td (- Lexi, extremely embarrassed) Tj
